Restore the citation pin, and carry the supervisor correction

`journal/autumn-ryan` **ca2fab7 -> e019691** (cite-autumn-ryan `main`). One line.

## What happened

The pin went **backwards**, in a commit about something else.

```
69c5908  Roll the citation pin forward to include the End Matter   -> c82e81a   (#104)
803812b  Record the image-exhibit design as a proto-issue          -> ca2fab7   (regressed)
```

`803812b` is a proto-issue document. It also moved a submodule pointer, almost certainly from a stale local checkout swept up by a broad `git add`. That silently reverted #104 and left the recorded pin **3 behind** `main`.

## Why it matters more than a stale pin usually does

The three commits it dropped include **tiliv/cite-autumn-ryan#3** — the supervisor's inverted line, marked. Verified directly:

- at the currently recorded pin `ca2fab7`: the marked line is **absent**
- at cite `main` `e019691`: **present**

So as it stands this node publishes the uncorrected quote — a named third party rendered saying the opposite of what he said, with the correction sitting merged upstream and unadopted. That is the one defect in that piece nobody wanted left standing.

## Also fixed upstream, not here

The End Matter's second claim (that the transcript garbled "Omri" into "A U M R I") was **withdrawn** in the same upstream PR: she asked him to spell it and that is him spelling it. Correcting it would have misspelled a real man against his own spoken spelling. That withdrawal rides along with this pin too.

## What this PR does NOT touch

`.journal-engine` is already correct. Its **recorded** pin on `main` is `34a7bfb` — current engine main, `frame-src 'self'` included. Only the *working checkout* in the main tree is stale at `58e6a0d`, which is local hygiene (`git submodule update`), not a deploy decision, and does not gate anything.

## Verified

Pin ancestry checked (`ca2fab7` is an ancestor of `e019691`, 3 behind; no divergence), and the presence/absence of the marked line confirmed at both commits.
